    "source_checks": "REGULARIZE.md reports every one of the lists' 324 certificates VALID under the source's two exact checkers, verify_cert.py and verify_cert2.py, and verified at 80 digits; the checkers are byte-identical to the copies the issue-399 packet retains. It calls each refreshed side the exact optimum of the store's best packing, and classes each of the fifteen as level 2, same packing traversable without expansion, by a path test that samples angle paths in 0.01 degree steps and that it says is not a continuous proof. Those statements are the author's; no source program ran here.",
    "credit": "Credit the packings to their finders, as the record holds them: Ryan Xu's (ry-xu, https://github.com/ry-xu/square_packing, issue 432) at 70, 102, 123, 129, 146 and 295, which at 70 Eric Deleeuw had refined (issue 483); Mishapolk's at 103 and 258 (issue 470), refinements of Ryan Xu's and of SQUISH's; and Nate Chaoweeraprasit's SQUISH packings of issue 481 at 153, 236, 263, 269, 292, 302 and 303, composed from pieces of Francisco Couzo's, Ryan Xu's and earlier packings. Evan Daniel (https://github.com/evand/square-packing) refreshed each from his store, solved it to the exact side stated, regularized it for display at that side and wrote the certificate. His lists name instead the finders of the arrangements the packings descend from: Joe DeVincentis at 70, Francisco Couzo at 102, 103, 123, 236, 263, 269, 292, 302 and 303, David Ellsworth at 129 and 153 and David W. Cantrell at 146, and no one at 258 and 295. The source claims no record, and its credits say the repository's work was produced by Claude (Anthropic) under human direction.",
    "next_rung": "Independently review the retained replay and the third route's reading, then weigh adoption count by count. Each side lies below every value the record holds or has pending, by 2.2e-17 at 302 to 7.8e-10 at 295; the source calls each the exact optimum of its store's best packing, and the credit takes that packing to be the one whose side lies just above. The regularized views differ from those certificates pose by pose, and that each is still the same packing is the source's sampled path test, not verified here; the review should decide whether the credit may rest on it. Then record source-specific adoption and confirming evidence. Final exact-head CI remains required.",
